Guard curl_close() calls behind a PHP < 8.0 check.

curl_close() has been a no-op since PHP 8.0 and is deprecated as of PHP 8.5,
where Magento's developer-mode error handler escalates the E_DEPRECATED notice
to a fatal exception (e.g. loading Adyen merchant accounts in admin). The call
is only meaningful on PHP 7.x, so guard it. Upstream: adyen/php-api-library.

--- a/src/Adyen/HttpClient/CurlClient.php
+++ b/src/Adyen/HttpClient/CurlClient.php
@@ -147,7 +147,9 @@
         // Get errors
         [$errno] = $this->curlError($ch);

-        curl_close($ch);
+        if (\PHP_VERSION_ID < 80000) {
+            curl_close($ch);
+        }

         $resultOKHttpStatusCodes = array(200, 201, 202, 204);

@@ -353,7 +355,9 @@
         // Get errors
         [$errno] = $this->curlError($ch);

-        curl_close($ch);
+        if (\PHP_VERSION_ID < 80000) {
+            curl_close($ch);
+        }

         $hasFailed = !in_array($httpStatus, array(200, 201, 202, 204));
